From: Kernel Hive lab <lab@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] cirrus: fix ISA vmstate to descend into the embedded CirrusVGAState

The ISA Cirrus device (`isa-cirrus-vga`) pointed `dc->vmsd` straight at
`vmstate_cirrus_vga`.  That VMSD's fields are declared against `CirrusVGAState`
(e.g. `VMSTATE_UINT8(cirrus_hidden_dac_data, CirrusVGAState)`), but a device's
vmsd is resolved against the *device* object.  For the ISA device that object
is `ISACirrusVGAState { ISADevice parent_obj; CirrusVGAState cirrus_vga; }`,
where `cirrus_vga` sits 160 bytes past the base (measured on this build).  So
every field was saved and restored 160 bytes off.

The `VGACommonState`-relative fields happened to round-trip (their offsets from
the wrong base still landed on live, stable memory), which masked the bug for
low-colour modes such as the nt351 tile.  But the cirrus-direct fields --
`cirrus_hidden_dac_data`, `cirrus_hidden_dac_lockindex`, `cirrus_shadow_gr0/1`
-- were saved and restored from the wrong location.  For the nt4 hi-res hybrid
(i440fx + isa-cirrus-vga at 1024x768x16bpp) this dropped the hidden-DAC depth
selector on `loadvm`: `cirrus_get_bpp16_depth()` fell back from 16bpp (565) to
15bpp (555), reinterpreting the restored framebuffer one green bit off -- the
deterministic blue/lavender corruption seen on both KVM and TCG.

Fix it exactly like the PCI variant (`vmstate_pci_cirrus_vga`): wrap the device
vmsd in a `VMSTATE_STRUCT` that descends into the `cirrus_vga` member, so the
substate opaque is the real `CirrusVGAState`.  The wire format and the section
name ("cirrus_vga") are unchanged; a fresh-process `loadvm golden` now restores
a byte-identical 1024x768x16bpp framebuffer (verified KVM+TCG, 3x each).

Proven with an instrumented build: pre-save `cirrus_hidden_dac_data=0xe1`
(565), post-restore `0x00` (reset) before the fix; `0xe1` after.  The
save/restore opaque delta was 160 before the fix and 0 after.
---
 hw/display/cirrus_vga_isa.c | 26 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/display/cirrus_vga_isa.c b/hw/display/cirrus_vga_isa.c
index 3d2b1a0c4e..7f8e9a0b1c 100644
--- a/hw/display/cirrus_vga_isa.c
+++ b/hw/display/cirrus_vga_isa.c
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 #include "hw/core/loader.h"
 #include "hw/core/qdev-properties.h"
 #include "hw/isa/isa.h"
+#include "migration/vmstate.h"
 #include "cirrus_vga_internal.h"
 #include "qom/object.h"
 #include "ui/console.h"
@@ -77,11 +78,35 @@
                      cirrus_vga.vga.global_vmstate, false),
 };
 
+/*
+ * vmstate fix (angle=trace): the ISA device's vmsd must descend into the
+ * embedded CirrusVGAState.  Pointing dc->vmsd straight at vmstate_cirrus_vga
+ * resolves that VMSD's CirrusVGAState field offsets against the *device*
+ * (ISACirrusVGAState) base, which is 160 bytes before cirrus_vga.  The
+ * VGACommonState-relative fields still round-tripped, but the cirrus-direct
+ * fields (cirrus_hidden_dac_data / _lockindex, cirrus_shadow_gr0/1) were saved
+ * and restored from the wrong location, so the hi-colour DAC depth was lost on
+ * loadvm (16bpp 565 -> 15bpp 555 = the blue/lavender corruption).  Wrap exactly
+ * like the PCI variant (vmstate_pci_cirrus_vga) so the substate opaque is the
+ * real CirrusVGAState.  Wire format and section name ("cirrus_vga") are
+ * unchanged.
+ */
+static const VMStateDescription vmstate_isa_cirrus_vga = {
+    .name = "cirrus_vga",
+    .version_id = 2,
+    .minimum_version_id = 1,
+    .fields = (const VMStateField[]) {
+        VMSTATE_STRUCT(cirrus_vga, ISACirrusVGAState, 0,
+                       vmstate_cirrus_vga, CirrusVGAState),
+        VMSTATE_END_OF_LIST()
+    }
+};
+
 static void isa_cirrus_vga_class_init(ObjectClass *klass, const void *data)
 {
     DeviceClass *dc = DEVICE_CLASS(klass);
 
-    dc->vmsd  = &vmstate_cirrus_vga;
+    dc->vmsd  = &vmstate_isa_cirrus_vga;
     dc->realize = isa_cirrus_vga_realizefn;
     device_class_set_props(dc, isa_cirrus_vga_properties);
     set_bit(DEVICE_CATEGORY_DISPLAY, dc->categories);
-- 
